{"id":1295,"date":"2020-11-26T16:42:53","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T00:42:53","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1295"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:46","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:46","slug":"build-the-soccer-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-soccer-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Soccer Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c382\" name=\"6a22165d9c382\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The body (bottom)<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this entire step, pay attention to the orientation of the blueboard and placement of the parts!<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Screw a bolt into the opening of a short standoff, and then attach the standoff to the middle of the blueboard&#8217;s bottom row.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to the two holes in the top righthand corner of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames to the top row of the blueboard. One should be on top of the long L-frame.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to the two holes in the top lefthand corner of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two long L-frames in the 6th row of the blueboard so they are\u00a0parallel to the top long L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two long standoffs in the third and fifth holes of the 2nd row of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1296&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1297&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1298&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c493\" name=\"6a22165d9c493\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Battery box<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the battery box to the two short standoffs on the blueboard.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1299&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c501\" name=\"6a22165d9c501\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The body (top)<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this entire step, pay attention to the orientation of the\u00a0blueboard\u00a0and placement of the parts!<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two long L-frames to the second and sixth columns of the blueboard. The ends that are sticking up in the air should be facing away from the center of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a 7-hole metal frame to each side of the blueboard so that they cross the long L-frames. Four holes from each frame should be sticking out off the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to the end of each 7-hole metal frame.\u00a0The ends that are sticking up in the air should be facing away from the center of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a 4-hole metal frame to each new long L-frame, and then bolt each 4-hole metal frame to the second to last holes from the bottom corners. You may need to move the L-frames to do this.<\/li>\n<li>Flip the whole thing over!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1300&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c558\" name=\"6a22165d9c558\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Combining the body<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Place the top half of the body onto the long standoffs on the bottom half of the body.<\/li>\n<li>Secure everything using two short standoffs.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1301&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c5b3\" name=\"6a22165d9c5b3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The grill<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt three 7-hole metal frames to two 7-hole metal frames so that the three frames are parallel to each other. They should be attached to every other hole on the two 7-hole metal frames, with the top and bottom holes left open.<\/li>\n<li>Use another 7-hole metal frame to attach a horn bracket to the center of the metal frames. This frame should be parallel to the two 7-hole metal frames. Use a long bolt for this part!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the center of the metal frame grid to the middle two long L-frames on the top half of the body.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1302&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1303&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1304&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c60d\" name=\"6a22165d9c60d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Shields, motors, and Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt a blueboard to each angled long L-frame on the top half of the body.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the motors to the long L-frames on the bottom half of the body.<\/li>\n<li>Use black screws to attach the wheels to the motors. The wheels will still stay on without the black screws!<\/li>\n<li>Use the two short standoffs on the top half of the body to attach the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1305&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1306&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1307&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1308&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c666\" name=\"6a22165d9c666\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Soccer Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To wire your Soccer Bot, make sure that the Smart Inventor Board is facing you:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1309&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1310&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165d9c6b7\" name=\"6a22165d9c6b7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How to use the Soccer Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Watch the video to see how your Soccer Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=gYS3pIiSXPQ&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 The body (bottom) [vc_column_text]For this entire step, pay attention to the orientation of the blueboard and placement of the parts! Screw a bolt into the opening of&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-soccer-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1740,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2172,2171,2210],"class_list":["post-1295","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-soccer-bot","module-soccer","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1295","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1295\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1311,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1295\/revisions\/1311"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1740"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1295"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/w